# A build context is copied wholesale to the daemon, whether or not a COPY names
# it. Without this file recall's context is the entire working tree: 1.5 GB of
# .venv, the mode-600 .env, and data/ — real recordings and real transcripts of
# real conversations. None of it is referenced by the Dockerfile, and all of it
# was being handed over anyway.
#
# CI never saw this: it builds from a clean checkout, where every path below is
# either gitignored or absent. The exposure is local, which is exactly why it is
# worth naming rather than trusting the Dockerfile's COPY lines to be enough.

# Secrets and runtime data — the reason this file exists.
.env
data/
audio/
logs/
work/
*.wav
*.flac
*.opus
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db

# Installed trees and build output. The frontend stage installs its own
# dependencies in a layer of its own; without this, the later `COPY frontend/ ./`
# puts the developer's node_modules straight back on top of it. pnpm's
# node_modules is a tree of symlinks into node_modules/.pnpm, which does not
# survive being copied out of context — so this stops being a wasted layer and
# starts being a broken build.
.venv/
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
frontend/.angular/
__pycache__/
*.egg-info/
result
result-*

# Caches and platform sources the image has no use for.
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
android/
ios/
.git/
